    {
      "id": "environment-meaning",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Meaning",
      "position": {
        "x": 20,
        "y": -1526
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Meaning",
        "body": "**What is this thing?** An environment is the room a graph's interior sits in: paper, a blueprint, a poster with a stage for the graph. It is drawn beneath every node and edge of the open graph, the ground included. It is not part of how the graph looks from outside, and it is not what you land on.\n\nEncoding: an ordinary face holding html, joined to the root by one `environment` edge from the root's `environment` port.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
